*** Add File:README_AEGIS_PAN_PILOTS.md
+# Aegis — Palo Alto Networks Pilot Suite (Unified Patch)
+
+This patch bundles multiple artifacts to run the PAN pilot:
+
+- Appliance agent SDK (Go) and Dockerfile to run signed models and verify attenstions before loading.
+- Panorama plugin (Flask) that displays evidence, allows requesting HIL, and links to evidence bundles stored in MCP.
+- CI workflow (GitHub Actions) using OIDC -> Vault login, calls receipt_signer (Vault Transit) to sign artifacts, optionally posts Rekor, generates evidence bundle and uploads to Cortex.
+- Federated starter (TFF orchestrator stub) and secure-aggregation integration guidance.
+- DP integration example using diffprivlib to apply rigorous DP with epsilon parameterization.
+- Enrollment helper for Vault-based client token issuance.
+- Evidence bundle generator specialized for PAN and attach-to-Cortex script.
+- Cortex XSOAR playbook sample that attaches evidence and requires HIL before remediation.
+- Kubernetes manifests to run Panorama plugin; operator should build/push the image aegis/panorama-plugin:latest.
+
+Operator next steps (high-level):
+1. Configure Vault (HA + auto-unseal), create transit key and receipt_signer (see earlier patches).
+2. Deploy Rekor with TLS and persistent DB; configure RECEIPT_SIGNER_URL and REKOR_URL in CI secrets.
+3. Build and push appliance agent image; provision devices and set /etc/aegis/agent_config.json with artifact/attest endpoints.
+4. Deploy Panorama plugin and secure it behind Panorama or corporate SSO.
+5. Run federated pilot using TFF or selected secure-aggregation library; use diffprivlib to test DP settings and utility.
+6. Integrate Cortex incident flows to attach evidence bundles and require HIL before automated remediation.
+
+Security & compliance notes:
+- Use Vault OIDC for CI and Vault Kubernetes auth or Vault Agent on appliances; avoid long-lived tokens.
+- Rekor must run with TLS and Postgres backend; configure backups and monitoring.
+- For federated flows, choose a vetted secure-aggregation library and perform threat modelling & security review.
+
